Note: Deferred work. if, and and or evaluate only what they need, so an
Note: expensive or failing branch is never touched when it is not taken.
use "@std"

Ints data = (list 4 8 15 16 23 42)

Note: and only evaluates its lazy second operand when the first is true.
proc safeAt (Ints: xs, Int: i)
    (if (and (gte i 0) lazy ((lt i (len xs)))) lazy (xs@i) lazy ((neg 1)))
end proc

(print (str (safeAt data 2)))
(print (str (safeAt data 99)))

Note: The untaken branch would fail, but it is never evaluated.
(print (if (empty data) lazy ((head (list))) lazy ("data present")))

Note: or stops at the first true operand.
(print (str (or (contains data 15) lazy ((print "not evaluated")))))

Note: An inline thunk runs only when forced.
(print (str (eval lazy ((reduce data 0 (fn Int a, Int x => (add a x)))))))

Note: A stored thunk runs once, however often it is forced.
Lazy total = lazy ((print "computing total..."))
(eval total)
(eval total)
